# Lecture 10B

## Karyotypes

## Chapter 9

## Dr. Neil Voss

## November 10, 2026

=== layout: bookend

# Learning Objectives

@body

- Explain how a karyotype is prepared from condensed chromosomes.
- Compare chromosome banding with fluorescent chromosome painting.
- Classify chromosome shapes by centromere position.
- Describe the origin and research importance of HeLa cells.

=== layout: section

# Welcome to Chapter 9

=== layout: one-panel
@replaceme

# *Abnormalities*

@body

- We study some of the chromosomal abnormalities encounter in human beings and other animals and plants
- In general animals are much less tolerant of chromosomal changes than are plants.
- Duplication of entire sets of chromosomes is not necessarily harmful in plants.

=== layout: one-panel

# *Sets of Chromosomes in Human Cells*

@body

- Human somatic cells have 23 pairs of chromosomes
- A [*karyotype*]{color=red} is an ordered display of the pairs of chromosomes from a cell

